            For a standard concrete or clay paver patio, Alliance Gator Maxx G2 is the safest all-round choice: easy to find, forgiving, and available in the colors most pavers need. Pay more for Techniseal HP NextGel if your pavers are smooth, light or already sealed and haze would be hard to live with. For flagstone and natural stone with wide joints, skip paver sand entirely and use GatorDust or Techniseal RG+.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever bag you buy, the installation decides the result more than the brand. Measure your joints, match the product to them, start only on dry pavers with a dry forecast, clean the surface completely, and mist patiently. Do that, and almost any of these sands will give you firm, weed-resistant joints for years.
          </p>
